                <pb facs="0902" n="790" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg790"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.032/42</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Fletcher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-25T12:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 25, 1918, noon.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1858. Chamber yesterday approved in general the President’s exercise of his
                    special powers in finance with the exception of decrees relative to public
                    charity and import tax on paper specifying duties in kind. Discussion of
                    particulars postponed until next week. Mail despatch mentioned in your 1740,
                    December 21, 7 p.m. has not been received.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
